  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light is incident at an angle of <math> <msup> <mtext>45</mtext> <mi>o</mi> </msup> </math> (relative to the normal) on a thin film of a liquid with an index of refraction of <math> <msqrt> <mtext>2</mtext></msqrt></math>. Assuming that the medium on both sides of the film is air, find the minimum thickness of the film required for constructive interference in the reflected light for sodium light of wavelength <math> <mn>600</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>nm</mtext></math>.<br />\r<u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0099_4f23a4e57800.jpg\" style=\"height: 171px; width: 250px;\" /></strong></u>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>122 nm</mtext></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>212 nm</mtext></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>173 nm</mtext></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>320 nm</mtext></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From Snell&#39;s law<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mtext>sin</mtext><msup><mtext>45</mtext><mtext>o</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math><br /><u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0099_4f23a4e57800.jpg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 171px;\" /></strong></u></p><p><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>r</mi></math><br /><br />For constructive interference in reflection<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>600&#160;nm</mtext><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mtext>cos30</mtext><mtext>o</mtext></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8776;</mo><mtext>122 nm</mtext></math></p>"
  }
}